# ek-editline: OPERATE the course editor -- place four control points so the course
# line (func_xk2_800E0988: L3DEX2 G_VTX(2)/PIPESYNC/PRIM/LINE3D per line) is drawn
# over the ground grid, then dwell. The [native] ek_editmesh receipt for the line half
# of the preview memo (ekeditmesh, o3dsek plan S5c); ek-widgetdrop and ek-courseedit
# only ever show the empty grid.
#
# EXPANSION-KIT-ONLY AND DISK-ONLY, exactly as ek-courseedit.gdxs explains. NOT a
# corpus replay, SHOTs hand-placed.
#
# Derivation (course_edit/188850.c):
#  - cursor starts at (160, 120); the stick moves it 2 px/tick at |stick| = 80
#    (ek-widgetdrop.gdxs derivation), stickX=+80 right, stickY=-80 down.
#  - with fewer than 4 points the editor is in CREATE COURSE / POINT SET
#    (func_xk2_800DB550 tail), so A with the cursor at y >= 56 places a point
#    (func_xk2_800DC67C) unless it lands on an existing one.
#  - the four points are the corners of a 80 x 50 px box: (160,120) (240,120)
#    (240,170) (160,170).
build native/ekeditline
seed1 0x1234abcd
seed2 0x0fedcba9
pins renderthread=1 bridgemain=1 det=1
note four control points on an 80x50 px box, then a dwell with the course line drawn.
at 350
wait 1
at 400
press START 15 0
at 600
wait 1
shot menu_before
at 660
press DOWN 12 0
at 760
wait 1
shot menu_cursor
at 820
press A 12 0
at 1100
wait 1
shot editor
at 1150
press A 12 0
at 1200
wait 1
shot pt1
at 1220
stick 80 0 20
at 1270
wait 1
shot mv1
at 1300
press A 12 0
at 1340
wait 1
shot pt2
at 1360
stick 0 -80 20
at 1395
wait 1
shot mv2
at 1420
press A 12 0
at 1460
wait 1
shot pt3
at 1480
stick -80 0 20
at 1530
wait 1
shot mv3
at 1560
press A 12 0
at 1700
wait 1
shot points_4
at 2100
wait 1
shot dwell_0
at 2500
wait 1
shot dwell_1
at 2900
wait 1
shot dwell_2
len 3000
